|                                                                                |
|    Velour features                                                             |
|                                                                                |
|    Velour is a BBS program. This is what it can do now.                        |
|                                                                                |
|    Connection                                                                  |
|                                                                                |
|    Guests come by telnet. Velour works with PuTTY, Tera Term and               |
|    inetutils telnet in a UTF-8 terminal.                                       |
|                                                                                |
|    Velour finds the terminal type, the terminal size and the colour            |
|    depth: 16, 256 or 16 million colours. The terminal needs the                |
|    UTF-8 charset. Without it, Velour tells the guest how to turn it            |
|    on.                                                                         |
|    ───────────────────────────   1/6   ────────────────────────────            |
|    Space Next                                           Esc To list            |
|                                                                                |
